    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Two different outputs for $x=1$, so it is not a function.",
      "worked": "At $x=1$, both $x\\ge 1$ and $x\\le 1$ hold.\n\nThe first rule gives $1$, while the second gives $1-1=0$.\n\nA function must assign exactly one output to each input in its domain. Here the same input has two different outputs, so this is not a valid function.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 20
